    "evenflo_faq_peRxwe": {
      "type": "evenflo-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_8rmhpB": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Is Shyft™ DualRide™ approved for use on aircraft?",
            "content": "<p>The Shyft™ DualRide™ is approved for use on an aircraft with the stroller wheels attached to the infant carrier. The base may not be used for installation on the aircraft. Please check with your airline before departure to make sure this car seat meets all requirements, including a minimum of 18 in. (45.7 cm) aisle width for use in stroller mode and a minimum of 18 in. (45.7 cm) aircraft seat width.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_4EfjBG": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Can I use this car seat on an aircraft?",
            "content": "<p>Yes, the Evenflo Shyft™ DualRide™ can be installed on an aircraft without the use of the base. NOTE: If the car seat is equipped with SensorSafe™, tighten the harness around your child and then unfasten the chest clip. In order to comply with the FAA regulation for Portable Electronic Devices, the SensorSafe™ chest clip must remain unfastened during take-off and landing.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_4Xjp8U": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Where can I find the sticker stating that my car seat is FAA approved?",
            "content": "<p>You can locate your car seat’s FAA compliance label underneath the infant carrier.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_GCcp7w": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Does this car seat fit into a travel bag?",
            "content": "<p>Yes, it fits in the Evenflo travel bag which can be purchased separately.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_MPz3gc": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "What’s the best way to travel with Shyft™ DualRide™ on an airplane?",
            "content": "<p>If you plan to use your car seat without the base on an aircraft, look for the label on the car seat stating that it is aircraft approved. There is also information in the user guide that states the Shyft™ DualRide™ is aircraft approved to be used without the base. You do not need to print or bring any additional information to use your car seat on an aircraft, however, it is a good practice to contact your airline prior to departure to make sure the car seat requirements for use on an aircraft, provided in your user guide, will be met.IIf you plan to use your car seat without the base on an aircraft, look for the label on the car seat stating that it is aircraft approved. There is also information in the user guide that states the Shyft™ DualRide™ is aircraft approved to be used without the base. You do not need to print or bring any additional information to use your car seat on an aircraft, however, it is a good practice to contact your airline prior to departure to make sure the car seat requirements for use on an aircraft, provided in your user guide, will be met.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_4i3tR4": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Can I use the Shyft™ DualRide™ for international travel?",
            "content": "<p>If you plan to fly internationally, ALWAYS check with the airline prior to departure to make sure the car seat requirements for use on an aircraft, provided in your user guide, will be met. The aircraft certification for the Shyft™ DualRide™ is only relevant for US or Canadian airlines that fall under the provisions of the Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) or Transport Canada (TC). International airlines may not allow car seat use on their aircraft or may have seating systems incompatible with your Shyft DualRide. Additionally, vehicles in other countries also meet different regulatory standards and may not have seating systems that are compatible with this car seat.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_gBHrxQ": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Can I purchase an airline ticket for my Shyft™ DualRide™?",
            "content": "<p>If you plan to use the Shyft™ DualRide™ on an aircraft for a child that is less than 2 years old, you must purchase a ticket for your child. You should contact the airline prior to departure to make sure the car seat requirements for use on an aircraft, provided in your user guide, will be met.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_HfM3RJ": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "The handle of my Shyft™ DualRide™ will not extend. What should I do?",
            "content": "<p>The Shyft™ DualRide™ handle will only extend when it is rotated into stroller mode. To rotate the handle, press both white buttons on the side of the handle and rotate the handle into stroller mode (towards your child’s feet). Then to extend the handle, press the white button in the center of the handle and pull the handle towards you.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_T8F3pG": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "The handle of my Shyft™ DualRide™ won’t rotate back into the carry position. What should I do?",
            "content": "<p>Your Shyft™ DualRide™ handle will only rotate when the handle is secured in the lowest locked position. Make sure the handle is fully locked into the shortest position (no silver should be showing near the sides of the handle grip). Once the handle is fully locked in place, you should be able to rotate the handle by pressing both white buttons on the side of the handle and pushing the handle to the upright carry position.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_jee8YF": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Can I fold and unfold the Shyft™ DualRide™ with the baby inside?",
            "content": "<p>Yes. The Shyft DualRide is designed to make travels with your infant easier and more convenient. You may keep your infant in the car seat while you fold or unfold the stroller wheels. Remember to keep your child snugly harnessed at all times when they are in the car seat.<br/><br/></p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_txwzcE": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Is the harness system removable or replaceable if my baby makes a mess?",
            "content": "<p>The harness system of this car seat is replaceable. However, the harness is easy to spot clean as needed using mild soap and warm water. For stubborn messes, a soft-bristle toothbruch may help with scrubbing. Take care not to soak the harness. The harness should then air dry.<br/><br/></p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_hzabVh": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "How do the Shyft™ DualRide™ brakes work?",
            "content": "<p>Your Shyft™ DualRide™’s rear wheels include a braking system for stroller mode. You’ll find one flip-flop-friendly brake on each rear wheel. You must press down on both brake pedals to fully lock the wheels against rolling. To release the brake, lift up on the brake pedal for each rear wheel. For safety, ALWAYS use the brakes when placing your child in or removing your child from the stroller — and ALWAYS check that both brakes are fully engaged.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_kDfJqJ": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "The wheels of my Shyft™ DualRide™ won’t move. What's wrong?",
            "content": "<p>If the wheels of your Shyft™ DualRide™ aren’t turning, double-check that both rear wheel brakes have been disengaged. To release the brake, lift up the brake pedal for each rear wheel. For safety, ALWAYS make sure both brakes are fully engaged when placing your child in or removing your child from the car seat.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_CUpq3y": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "What parts can be replaced on the Shyft™ DualRide™?",
            "content": "<p>The following parts may be replaced if needed: buckle cover, harness cover, seat pad, canopy, infant insert, front and rear wheels, wheel wells, stroller frame, cup holder, and cup holder clip. Replacement parts may be ordered at parts.evenflo.com or by contacting ParentLink from 8 am to 5 pm EST, Monday through Friday at 1-800-233-5921 (US) or 937-773-3971 (Canada).</p>"
          }
        }
      },
