    "evenflo_faq_hpTWkM": {
      "type": "evenflo-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_e7HPpV": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Why won’t my Shyft™ DualRide™ click into the base?",
            "content": "<p>If you’re having trouble getting your Shyft™ DualRide™ infant carrier with the stroller frame to click into your car seat base, make sure your stroller wheels with the stroller frame are properly folded and both wheels are aligned in an upright position. You may need to remove the infant carrier with the stroller frame, then unfold and refold the stroller wheels. Additionally, double-check the central front adjuster (CFA) strap between your child’s legs to make sure it is not blocking the connection to the base. An elastic loop is provided at the end of this strap so you can roll it up for out-of-the-way storage.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_wTwQcz": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "How do I know when the infant carrier with the frame is secure in the base?",
            "content": "<p>Listen for the tell-tale ‘click’ that lets you know your car seat base and infant carrier with stroller frame are fully attached — and ALWAYS lift up on the carrier handle to check that it’s secure. If you are having difficulty connecting your Shyft™ DualRide™ to the base, you may need to double-check that the stroller wheels are properly folded. Remove the infant carrier with the stroller frame, then unfold and refold your wheels, and try clicking into the base again. Also, be sure to double-check the central front adjuster (CFA) strap between your child’s legs to make sure it is not blocking the connection to the base. An elastic loop is provided at the end of this strap so you can roll it up for out-of-the-way storage.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_VKay4i": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "How do I know when to change the waist strap position for my baby?",
            "content": "<p>Include a helpful and informative answer to the frequently asked question here.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_MiLhqN": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "How do I know the recline is correct for my baby?",
            "content": "<p>Look for the bubble indicator at the top of your Shyft™ DualRide™’s infant car seat base. The bubble must be in the blue zone at all times to ensure that your child is properly positioned. To adjust the base to the correct position for your child, squeeze the recline handle and raise or lower the recline foot.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_fEDg8z": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Where do I check to make sure I have a tight install?",
            "content": "<p>Firmly grip the car seat near the belt path opening, which is where you have it installed. Try to move the car seat from side to side and front to back. The car seat should not move more than one inch (2.5 cm). If it moves more than one inch at the belt path, try your installation again. If it still moves more than one inch you may need to change seating positions in your vehicle or try   different installation method.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_T6zh9c": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "How do I know if my car seat is tightly installed?",
            "content": "<p>When checking for a tight installation, it is important to test the car seat right where you have it installed in the vehicle. For a rear-facing car seat, that means you will grab the car seat near your child's feet and not near their head. For an infant car seat secured with the base, make sure you test for tightness by grabbing the belt path on the base (not the infant carrier). If you have installed</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_zzcXgR": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Can I install the Evenflo Shyft™ DualRide™ in the center seat of my vehicle?",
            "content": "<p>Yes, the Evenflo Shyft™ DualRide™ can be used in any forward-facing vehicle seating position allowed in your vehicle’s owner’s manual, as long as a tight installation can be achieved. Therefore, the center seating position may be an option. However, in some vehicles, the center seating position may be narrower which could make it more difficult to tightly install your car seat. In many vehicles, the center seating position may not allow installation with lower anchors. It is important to refer to both your vehicle owner's manual and your car seat user guide for full installation details.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_DGMbDN": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "If I have both this car seat and a second car seat, will there be enough room to fit a third passenger in my backseat?",
            "content": "<p>There are many combinations of vehicle makes, models, car seat configurations, vehicle seat belt designs, and seat cushion shapes. The easiest way to determine whether your car seat is suitable for a particular seating position is to check for a tight installation, especially when trying to fit multiple passengers in the back seat of your vehicle. Unfortunately, some smaller sedans and SUVs have rear seat belt systems that overlap, which makes it very difficult to fit three passengers in the rear seat.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_PyUpwX": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Can I use a pool noodle or towel if I need more recline?",
            "content": "<p>Yes, in certain situations. The base of the Evenflo Shyft™ DualRide™ has 5 recline positions for rear-facing installations. There is a bubble level indicator on the top of the base; the bubble must be in the blue zone. Try to use the recline foot first to achieve the correct recline in your vehicle. If more reclining is needed, store the recline foot, and then tightly roll a towel or use a section of pool noodle underneath the base near the vehicle seat back to increase the recline angle, if necessary. You may also use the rolled towel or pool noodle if you are installing the infant carrier without the base.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_ALkW6B": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Can I use the LATCH/UAS system?",
            "content": "<p>Absolutely! The Evenflo Shyft™ DualRide™ comes equipped with QuickConnectors for a simple and secure installation. There is no weight limit for lower anchor use. You may install your Shyft™ DualRide™ using either the lower anchors or the vehicle seat belt.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
